  formidable so let me know there is one  more agent that's not here who robin and  brooke may have to deal with somehow but  those odds seem a lot better now than  when they had to deal with all three  then we jump to the most high part of  the chapter zoro vs king even though  king seemed like a very cool right hand  man to kaido he is not immune from oda's  dinosaur jokes in a not very cool  looking move king pulls his head back to  the point where it looks completely  unnatural he lets go like a slingshot  and zoro's surprised that he couldn't  block it since the attack is like a beam  like the dinocopter moment king says  that that's how tyrannodons hunted their  prey in prehistoric times that's just  been oda this arc confusing children  everywhere about how dinosaurs actually  work and of course zoro seemingly as  clueless as ever asks is that so if  anyone would believe it it's probably  zorro and luffy for that matter zoro  though is not in good shape here panting  and having trouble reaching the airborne  king in this case he's just wasting  energy with his attacks as king dodges  them he desperately needs a power up  here just like sanji got sora starts  asking questions that don't sound any  crazier than what king is saying like  that tyrannodons flew with fire on their  backs too but king says no that of  course seems to be part of his lunarian  genes as has been suggested zoro notices  that king is talking down to him and  decides he needs to knock him out of the  sky his great dragon twister is easily  blocked by king using his wings after  this zorro says that dinosaurs are a lot  like dragons king says he's not wrong  but king himself is on another level  that's a pretty arrogant thing to say  when someone compares your powers to  like the strongest creature ever but  king is backing it up here king even  takes pity on zorro and says he'll give  him a chance by using his sword instead  he's been craving a good duel as well  and here you really feel 